### 8. Term and termination

The right to run and operate the Software under Article 2(b) is
conditional on the existence of the User's active relationship with
the Service (an active account, trial, or subscription). Upon
termination of that relationship — cancellation of the account, expiry
of the trial without transition to a paid plan, termination of the
subscription, or deletion of the account under the terms of the
Service — that right ceases, and the User is obliged, without undue
delay and no later than within 30 days, to stop operating the Software
and to **remove it from all of the User's devices and servers**. The
right to view the published source code under Article 2(a) remains
unaffected.

The rights under this License further cease at the moment of their
breach by the User. The Provider may also revoke them with 30 days'
notice by publication in the repository; this does not affect a
running subscription to the Service under its terms. After the rights
cease, the removal obligation under the preceding paragraph applies
accordingly; the provisions of Articles 4, 6, and 7 survive
termination.

### 9. Governing law and dispute resolution

This License is governed by the law of the Czech Republic.

Disputes with a User who is **not a consumer** shall, to the exclusion
of the jurisdiction of the ordinary courts, be finally resolved in
arbitration before the Arbitration Court attached to the Czech Chamber
of Commerce and the Agricultural Chamber of the Czech Republic under
its rules, by a single arbitrator appointed in accordance with those
rules, with the seat of the proceedings in Prague and Czech as the
language of the proceedings.

Disputes with a User who **is a consumer** shall be resolved by the
ordinary courts; this is without prejudice to mandatory consumer
protection provisions of the country of the consumer's habitual
residence. A consumer is entitled to use out-of-court resolution of
consumer disputes, for which the competent body is the Czech Trade
Inspection Authority (www.coi.cz).

